    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d422">

                <pb facs="0325" n="321" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg321"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/3173: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lochhart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-14T14:00:00-04:00">May 14, 1938—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>318. Your 658, May 13,7 p.m. Department approves your proposed action and
                    suggests that in drafting your reply you also be guided by the ante-penultimate
                    paragraph of the Department’s 63, February 18, 5 p.m.<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d422-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d422-f1" n="16" xml:id="d422-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; for note of February 21, from the American Ambassador in Japan to
                    the Japanese Minister for Foreign Affairs, see <ref
                        target="frus1931-41v01#pg_586"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >i</hi>, p. 586</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
